WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.234
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book two.

2
00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.711
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.011 --> 00:00:15.124
Unit sixteen: Career Dreams. Today you will talk about future careers with hope to and plan to.

4
00:00:15.424 --> 00:00:18.041
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.581
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:23.417 --> 00:00:24.313
Profession.

7
00:00:25.317 --> 00:00:28.106
Profession means a job that needs special training.

8
00:00:28.717 --> 00:00:31.053
Medicine is a respected profession.

9
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:34.360
Your turn. Say: Profession.

10
00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.201
Profession.

11
00:00:38.950 --> 00:00:39.986
Internship.

12
00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:44.283
Internship means a short period of work to get experience.

13
00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:46.732
She did an internship at a bank.

14
00:00:47.317 --> 00:00:50.015
Your turn. Say: Internship.

15
00:00:52.867 --> 00:00:53.984
Internship.

16
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:55.925
Qualification.

17
00:00:56.917 --> 00:01:00.472
Qualification means a certificate or degree you get after study.

18
00:01:01.083 --> 00:01:03.524
You need a qualification to be a nurse.

19
00:01:04.117 --> 00:01:07.071
Your turn. Say: Qualification.

20
00:01:09.933 --> 00:01:11.260
Qualification.

21
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:13.285
Passion project.

22
00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:17.943
Passion project means work you do because you love it.

23
00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:20.921
My passion project is a cooking blog.

24
00:01:21.517 --> 00:01:24.215
Your turn. Say: Passion project.

25
00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.474
Passion project.

26
00:01:29.217 --> 00:01:30.113
Role model.

27
00:01:31.117 --> 00:01:34.312
Role model means a person you admire and want to be like.

28
00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:36.580
My aunt is my role model.

29
00:01:37.183 --> 00:01:39.836
Your turn. Say: Role model.

30
00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:43.945
Role model.

31
00:01:44.683 --> 00:01:45.777
Skillset.

32
00:01:46.783 --> 00:01:49.387
Skillset means all the skills a person has.

33
00:01:49.983 --> 00:01:51.925
Coding is part of my skillset.

34
00:01:52.517 --> 00:01:54.832
Your turn. Say: Skillset.

35
00:01:57.667 --> 00:01:58.877
Skillset.

36
00:01:59.617 --> 00:02:00.745
Opportunity.

37
00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:04.527
Opportunity means a chance to do something good.

38
00:02:05.117 --> 00:02:07.639
This scholarship is a great opportunity.

39
00:02:08.250 --> 00:02:11.030
Your turn. Say: Opportunity.

40
00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:14.903
Opportunity.

41
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:16.767
Mentor.

42
00:02:17.783 --> 00:02:20.665
Mentor means an experienced person who guides you.

43
00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:23.203
My mentor gives me good advice.

44
00:02:23.817 --> 00:02:26.690
Your turn. Say: Mentor.

45
00:02:29.533 --> 00:02:30.558
Mentor.

46
00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:32.712
Work experience.

47
00:02:33.717 --> 00:02:37.040
Work experience means time spent doing a real job.

48
00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:39.835
Work experience helps you get a job.

49
00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:43.346
Your turn. Say: Work experience.

50
00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.770
Work experience.

51
00:02:48.517 --> 00:02:49.634
Industry.

52
00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:53.300
Industry means all the businesses of one type.

53
00:02:53.883 --> 00:02:56.684
The tourism industry is growing in Cambodia.

54
00:02:57.283 --> 00:02:59.750
Your turn. Say: Industry.

55
00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:03.566
Industry.

56
00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:05.364
Ambitious.

57
00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:08.895
Ambitious means wanting very much to succeed.

58
00:03:09.483 --> 00:03:11.483
She is ambitious and works hard.

59
00:03:12.083 --> 00:03:14.829
Your turn. Say: Ambitious.

60
00:03:17.667 --> 00:03:18.737
Ambitious.

61
00:03:19.483 --> 00:03:20.345
Pathway.

62
00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:23.942
Pathway means a way or plan to reach a goal.

63
00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:27.374
University is one pathway to a career.

64
00:03:27.983 --> 00:03:30.496
Your turn. Say: Pathway.

65
00:03:33.333 --> 00:03:34.381
Pathway.

66
00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:39.119
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:39.983 --> 00:03:42.343
Visal, what career would you like to pursue?

68
00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.844
I hope to become a software engineer.

69
00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.183
Who inspired you?

70
00:03:49.283 --> 00:03:53.433
My cousin. He's my role model and my mentor.

71
00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:55.783
What's your plan?

72
00:03:56.883 --> 00:04:03.121
I plan to study IT at university, and I hope to find an internship to gain work experience.

73
00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:05.895
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:06.750 --> 00:04:09.574
Grammar focus: hope to and plan to.

75
00:04:09.874 --> 00:04:11.049
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:11.750 --> 00:04:13.691
I hope to find an internship.

77
00:04:14.583 --> 00:04:16.757
I plan to gain work experience.

78
00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:19.406
She hopes to become a doctor.

79
00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:24.610
'Hope to' is for wishes. 'Plan to' is for things you have decided to do.

80
00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:29.337
Be careful! Don't say: I plan getting an internship.

81
00:04:31.300 --> 00:04:33.845
Say: I plan to get an internship.

82
00:04:34.145 --> 00:04:36.667
Use 'to' plus a verb after 'hope' and 'plan'.

83
00:04:37.467 --> 00:04:40.351
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:41.167 --> 00:04:42.342
My Pathway.

85
00:04:42.642 --> 00:04:45.802
My role model, my aunt, inspired my career dreams.

86
00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.344
She works in the tourism industry, and she is very ambitious.

87
00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:54.598
I plan to get a good qualification and build my skillset.

88
00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:58.575
I hope an internship will give me work experience.

89
00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:03.122
With a mentor's help, I will find a clear pathway in this industry.

90
00:05:04.233 --> 00:05:08.351
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:09.217 --> 00:05:11.495
I plan blank IT at university.

92
00:05:11.795 --> 00:05:15.471
A, to study. B, study. C, studying.

93
00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:20.661
The answer is A: to study.

94
00:05:21.817 --> 00:05:25.024
A short period of work to get experience is an blank.

95
00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:29.012
A, internship. B, industry. C, mentor.

96
00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:34.764
The answer is A: internship.

97
00:05:35.917 --> 00:05:38.090
Wanting very much to succeed is blank.

98
00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:42.508
A, ambitious. B, qualified. C, passionate.

99
00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:48.078
The answer is A: ambitious.

100
00:05:49.267 --> 00:05:52.685
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:56.049
What career would you like to pursue and why?

102
00:06:04.850 --> 00:06:06.362
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:06.662 --> 00:06:15.897
I would like to be a teacher. I hope to help children in my village, and I plan to study English and education at university.

104
00:06:16.197 --> 00:06:17.976
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:18.883 --> 00:06:23.173
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and hope to and plan to.

106
00:06:23.473 --> 00:06:27.437
Today's value is ambition. Dream big and work hard for your future.

107
00:06:27.737 --> 00:06:30.587
See you in Unit seventeen. Goodbye!

108
00:06:30.887 --> 00:06:33.992
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

